<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/devLifecycleStage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The development lifecycle stage specifies the phase or phases of a product’s lifecycle to which a given requirement applies. These may include requirements that govern the design phase, guide development activities, define constraints for the build environment, provide instructions for the decommissioning phase, etc."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Extension/cdxPropValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A cdxPropValue is used in a CdxPropertyEntry name-value pair.\n\nUnlike key-value stores, properties in CdxPropertiesExtension support duplicate\nnames, each potentially having different values."@en .
